# Architecture Rules (P1) — Core Architectural Decisions

## A-1 — 3-Layer Agent Hierarchy (P1–P5)

The dispatcher boundary is defined by S-1. S-1 applies to Project→Wave→Task:
L0/L1 dispatch only; L2 executes within ~8K; L0/L1 receive ~5K. Inter-layer
messages MUST use typed YAML (TaskDispatch, StatusReport, ExceptionEscalation);
free-form messages are prohibited. Every loop has `max_iterations`; failures
classify as retry/escalate/abort and escalate Task→Wave→Project→Human.
Artifacts are typed, producer-written contracts; no shared/bidirectional state.

## A-2 — P6 Preserve Cached Prefix (Cache-Layout Governance v2)

Dispatch payloads MUST honor `schemas/lean-dispatch.yaml#layout_invariant`;
call `devolaflow.compressor.assert_dispatch_layout(payload)` before sending.
New top-level keys MUST append after position 17 in the live schema; reordering is a release
blocker.

### A-2.1 — Frozen Prefix (positions 1-12)

The first 12 `canonical_order` positions are the **FROZEN PREFIX** and their
byte-stable rendering is the LLM cache prefix. Reordering, renaming, or
removing one is a release blocker; enforce with
`devolaflow.compressor.assert_layout_spec_invariant`.

### A-2.2 — Append-Only Tail (positions 13+)

Positions 13+ are **APPEND-ONLY**: new top-level keys land at N+1, never lower.

### A-2.3 — Nest-vs-Append Decision Rule

Per v9-ADR-002 D3, **NEST** when behavior modifies/reuses an existing block or
is co-present; **APPEND** only for orthogonal/cross-block state. Independently
optional fields may use either, but prefer NEST; every append can extend the
serialized cache prefix.

### A-2.4 — Multi-Baseline Byte Test (Tiered Retention)

CI runs `tests/test_layout_invariant_multi_baseline.py` against
`layout_invariant_v*.yaml`; witness drift fails. Schema bumps add a new golden
and retain every existing witness.

* **Tier A** immutable layout witnesses in
  `benchmarks/devolaflow_context/baselines/`.
* **Tier B** current + previous two
  `.local/telemetry/baselines/harness_baseline_<cycle>.json`.
* **Tier C** older baselines in
  `docs/cycle-archive/<cycle>/harness/`; history is retained.

## A-3 — Context Token Budgets

`workflow-system/agent/context_profiles.yaml` MUST define explicit per-task
budgets, allocated by priority: critical, then important, then supplementary.
Layer budgets: L0 Project ~5K (template/status), L1 Wave ~5K
(tasks/dependencies/evidence), L2 Task ~8K (spec/owned files/rules).

## A-4 — Source-of-Truth Spec Location (M-004 ADR)

`.local/memory/specs/<domain>/spec.md` is behavioral SSOT; per-change
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/spec.md` contains ADDED/MODIFIED/REMOVED deltas.
SSOT mutates ONLY at archive time after a passed gate (W-3/SI-3 ≥8.5 minor,
≥9.0 major); its `mergeability_check` (v8.2.5 reporter) must pass before merge.

## A-5 — Single-Source-of-Truth Registry Pattern

Every domain registry surface MUST have **exactly one owner module**. Consumers
import its registration data and MUST NOT redefine or shadow it. Parity and
derived-view status are enforced by `tests/ghost/test_registries.py`.

| # | Registry surface | Owner module / file |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Plugin registry | `workflow-system/agent/knowledge/runtime-plugins.yaml`, loaded by `devolaflow.plugins.installer.load_registry`; `plugins.yaml` is a derived view, pinned by `tests/test_plugins.py::TestV15PluginRegistryUnification` |
| 2 | Memory-router case type | `src/devolaflow/memory_router/cache.py::MemoryCase` |
| 3 | Host Support Contract | `workflow-system/agent/hosts.yaml`, loaded by `devolaflow.host_contract.load_host_contract`; `manifest.yaml::install_profiles` is derived |
| 4 | Local archive adapters (registered surfaces and archive destinations) | `src/devolaflow/local/archive_adapters.py::ARCHIVE_ADAPTERS` |

### A-5.1 — Single-Owner Invariant

Adding a surface requires one owner and routing all consumers through it.
Splitting registration data invalidates cache reasoning and is a release
blocker. `tests/ghost/test_registries.py::test_registry_single_owner` uses an
AST walk to reject multiple module-level definitions.

### A-5.2 — DEFAULT_ALLOWLIST Hygiene

`DEFAULT_ALLOWLIST` covers public APIs without in-repo callers; SSOT registry
symbols MUST NOT appear there. Enforce with `_check_allowlist_domain_overlap`
and `tests/test_dead_apis.py`.

## A-6 — Workspace Engagement Auto-Activation

When `DEVOLAFLOW_AGENT_WORKSPACE=1` AND complexity ≥ STANDARD per the
SKILL.md §"Quick Action Decision" table, L0 MUST scaffold
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/` with `entrance.md` before dispatching the first
L1 stage.
Default-OFF; rule is normative for opted-in operators.

### A-6.1 — Classification surface
Complexity classification is the output of
`devolaflow.skills.change_activation.classify_complexity(...)`; the
activation verdict is `activation_verdict(complexity, env_flag,
opt_out)`. The three-valued verdict (MUST_OPEN_CHANGE /
SHOULD_OPEN_CHANGE / NO_CHANGE) is the sole public contract —
operators rely on the string values.

### A-6.2 — Opt-in gate
`DEVOLAFLOW_AGENT_WORKSPACE=1` is REUSED per W-20 (same activation
surface as v9.1.1 PV-01 SKILL.md §"Workspace Engagement (Read at
Session Start)" and as the v9.1.3 PV-03 `pre_handoff` hook will use).
NO new env flag. Absent or any value other than the literal string
"1" = default-OFF (R5 strict).

### A-6.3 — Opt-out escape hatch
Users may pass `--no-change` to `/devola:propose` to suppress
scaffolding even when the env flag is ON. No other opt-out channel
exists (keeps the surface auditable).

### A-6.4 — Enforcement
Prompt-side: SKILL.md §"Quick Action Decision" sub-table cites this
rule. CI-side: `tests/test_change_activation_heuristic.py` pins the
three verdict cases + opt-out behaviour + byte-stable no-op when env
flag absent.

### A-6.5 — Task/Change Folder Entrance Materialization
When an agent creates or opens a task/change folder under
`.local/.agent/active/<id>/` or `.local/tasks/<name>/`, `entrance.md` MUST be
written in the first artifact batch, unless the programmatic scaffold
(`scaffold_change_folder` / `Change.to_active_folder`) performs that write.

## A-7 — Cascade-Depth Invariant for Standard+ Dispatches

When `gate.cascade_required` is `true` (STANDARD/COMPLEX from
`devolaflow.skills.change_activation::cascade_requirement`), dispatch MUST
traverse at least `gate.cascade_min_layers` layers before L2 (default 3:
L0 Project→L1 Wave→L2 Task). SIMPLE/TRIVIAL returns
`"CASCADE_OPTIONAL"` and bypasses this rule.

### A-7.1 — Conditional strict enforcement

For `"CASCADE_REQUIRED"`, STRICT
`validate_cascade_gate_fields` returns `None` on pass and raises
`CascadeViolationError` on the first invalid field/depth violation; declared
`cascade_min_layers` is validated at face value. For `"CASCADE_OPTIONAL"`,
validation is skipped and legacy dispatches without fields remain byte-identical.

### A-7.2 — Trivial waiver

Per A-1 P1, L0 may directly author a single-file edit under 20 lines. At
payload level, omitted `gate.cascade_required` (v11.0.x default) skips
validation; `populate_cascade_gate_fields` returns an unchanged deep copy for
SIMPLE/TRIVIAL.

### A-7.3 — Operator override

`force_no_change=True` bypasses workspace activation and is orthogonal to A-7.

### A-7.4 — Enforcement surface

* Tests: `tests/test_cascade_enforcement.py` covers strict, compatibility,
  skip, propagation, and immutability.
* Runtime: `validate_cascade_gate_fields` returns `None` or raises
  `CascadeViolationError`; `populate_cascade_gate_fields` defaults to 3.
* Audit: `scripts/audit_layer_usage.py --threshold N` is strict by default
  (exit 1 below `cascade_ratio` N); `--no-strict` opts out; default N=0.30.
* Schema: `gate.cascade_required: bool` and `gate.cascade_min_layers: int`
  nest under `gate`; absence is canonical.
